WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.132
The bugs used to attack my base. This time,
I went into their burrow

2
00:00:04.312 --> 00:00:05.282
to attack the queen!

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.220
An early gameplay run of Swarm Siege.
Recorded on October fourth.

4
00:00:11.675 --> 00:00:14.858
The visuals, controls and gameplay had just
changed.

5
00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:16.720
Here is one run through that earlier build,

6
00:00:16.912 --> 00:00:19.020
showing its defense and counterattack route.

7
00:00:20.783 --> 00:00:25.703
I head out as the medic. Aiming and firing
are automatic by default.

8
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:29.653
Positioning matters: get close enough, and
the character starts firing.

9
00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:32.366
Need some distance? Press Space to dash in
this build.

10
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.420
Third person shows the surroundings. V
switches to first person in this build.

11
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:44.107
Prefer manual controls? Shooting and
shortcuts are configurable.

12
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:50.541
There is no rush to start the wave. I clear
the abandoned supply station,

13
00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:54.153
collect the first-clear reward, then spend
the coins at the shop.

14
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.795
The machine gun gives sustained fire.

15
00:00:57.912 --> 00:01:01.482
A shotgun spreads pellets at close range.

16
00:01:01.937 --> 00:01:07.195
Stay near the blue beacon circle. Fight and
collect coins inside the area.

17
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:14.066
You can build your own defenses. Choose a
turret and check its preview.

18
00:01:14.346 --> 00:01:17.741
Confirm when the position looks right.
Placed it badly? Dismantle it

19
00:01:17.946 --> 00:01:19.228
for half the construction cost back.

20
00:01:21.017 --> 00:01:23.712
I hire a teammate, then head for the elite
nest.

21
00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.624
The squad helps fight and collect supplies.

22
00:01:26.929 --> 00:01:29.812
Rewards pay for stronger equipment.

23
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:37.003
Enough coins for the pulse laser cannon. The
target is deep inside the map:

24
00:01:37.146 --> 00:01:38.366
the alien queen.

25
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:43.237
I follow the central burrow, using first
person to see the route.

26
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:47.887
Beyond the tunnel: the queen and guards. Do
not wait at the entrance.

27
00:01:48.129 --> 00:01:49.399
Move into firing range!

28
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:56.107
The beam keeps hitting, and damage numbers
appear. The guards can block the way.

29
00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.245
Clear the immediate threats, then keep
firing at the queen.

30
00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:05.562
Defeated! Later swarms shrink 35% in this
build.

31
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:08.712
Attacking first takes pressure off the base.

32
00:02:10.517 --> 00:02:13.874
Back at the front of the base, I intercept
bugs emerging from the burrow.

33
00:02:14.329 --> 00:02:18.612
The wave is cleared. Stage two begins with
the base at full health.

34
00:02:20.383 --> 00:02:24.528
More coins can buy a vehicle. I board with I
in this recorded build,

35
00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.003
then drive out for a different approach.

36
00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:31.003
From supplies and equipment

37
00:02:31.071 --> 00:02:34.466
to the queen: a complete gameplay route.

38
00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:39.903
Tunnel visibility and squad following still
needed work.

39
00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:42.628
Those were priorities in this early build.

40
00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:48.599
Recorded on October fourth. The current demo
is linked below.

41
00:02:48.842 --> 00:02:54.074
Follow its in-game controls. Would you
defend first, or attack the queen?
